# Data files — sensitive / large / OneDrive-synced, never commit
data/*.csv
data/*.tsv
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls

# UNTRACKED-EXCEPTION 2026-09-24 — `series_to_band.csv` is NOT a build output, it is the
# hand-authored mapping every banding script reads (`modules/vehicle_bands.py` is the only
# reader). Because `data/*.csv` excludes it, the single file the whole ladder depends on had
# no version history and could never be diffed against a committed state. This is a
# deliberately narrow exception: the other CSVs in this folder are generated and stay ignored.
!data/series_to_band.csv

# Allow production data files — private repo, needed for Streamlit Cloud
# !data/UIO.xlsx  # blocked at ISZE root — holiday laptop uses derived JSON
!data/distributor_master_mapping.csv
# UNTRACKED 2026-09-20 — this line was re-including line-level billing (44 MB of
# sold_to / billing_date / part_number / net_sales_value rows) into git. ISZE
# policy is never to commit raw billing, and the replacement is already tracked
# at 01_data/00_derived/sales_fact.parquet (REFERENCE.md maps this file to it).
# Kept commented so the decision is visible and reversible in one edit if a
# Streamlit Cloud deploy genuinely needs the TSV.
# !data/sales_detailed_for_claude_full_fixed.tsv
!data/dealer_sales/
!data/dealer_sales/**

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.env

# Streamlit cache
.streamlit/

# Local scratch / inspect output
*_out.txt
*_dump.txt
bvp_inspect_out.txt
data/_crossref_build_log.txt
data/_ituk_study_dump.txt
data/_crossref_build_runner.py
data/analyze_ituk.py
inspect_bvp.py

